.TH TOW 1 "September 2026" "tow 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tow \- a quick overview tree for unknown or forgotten projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tow
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tow
lists the contents of directories in a tree-like format, tuned for a quick
overview rather than an exhaustive listing.  Directories that hold many files
are collapsed: a few "exemplary" files of each type are shown and the remainder
is summarized (e.g. "\&... 7 more .py").
.PP
By default, files matched by
.B .gitignore
are shown; use the
.B \-\-gitignore
option to hide them.  Hidden files (those beginning with a dot) are not shown,
and directories are shown before files.  With no
.I PATH
argument, the current directory is listed.
.PP
Inside a git repository, each file is annotated with its last commit (short
hash, date, and trimmed subject).  See the
.B \-\-no\-commits
option to disable this.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Include hidden files.
.TP
.B \-\-gitignore
Respect .gitignore and hide ignored files (they are shown by default).
.TP
.BI \-L " N" "\fR, \fB\-\-max\-depth " N
Limit the depth of the tree.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-dirs\-only
List directories only.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-full\-path
Print the full path prefix for each entry.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Number of files shown per file type per directory (default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-select " MODE"
How to choose exemplary files: \fBimportant\fR (default), \fBrecent\fR,
\fBmodified\fR, or \fBname\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " KEY"
Order files by \fBname\fR, \fBmtime\fR, \fBcommits\fR, \fBsize\fR,
\fBversion\fR, or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-reverse
Reverse the sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-filesfirst
List files before directories.
.TP
.B \-\-commits
Annotate files with their last commit (default inside a repository).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-commits
Do not annotate files with their last commit.
.TP
.BI \-\-recent "[=N]"
Print a flat list of the N most recently committed files (default N=10).
.TP
.B \-\-full\-commits
Always show full commit info (hash, date, subject), without truncating to the
terminal width.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-size
Print the size of each file and directory in bytes.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-human
Print sizes in a human readable format (powers of 1024).
.TP
.B \-\-si
Like \fB\-h\fR but use SI units (powers of 1000).
.TP
.B \-\-du
Alias: report directory sizes (implied by \fB\-s\fR, \fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-si\fR).
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-date
Print the last modification date of each file.
.TP
.BI \-\-timefmt " FORMAT"
Format dates with strftime(3) syntax (implies \fB\-D\fR).
.TP
.BI \-P " PATTERN"
List only files matching the glob pattern (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-I " PATTERN"
Do not list files matching the glob pattern (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Prune empty directories from the output.
.TP
.B \-\-noreport
Omit the final file/directory report.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-important
Disable the "important files" boost.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-dirs
Show all directories (disable screen-fit collapsing).
.TP
.BI \-\-height " N"
Limit the tree to N lines, forcing collapsing even when output is not a
terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N"
Override the terminal width used to truncate commit annotations.
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-classify
Append a '/' to directories, '*' to executables, '@' to symlinks.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-noindent
Do not print indentation lines.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-follow
Follow symbolic links to directories.
.TP
.B \-C
Force color output even when not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-n
Disable color output.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
When to use color: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use this config file instead of the default user config.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore all config files (user and project).
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-config
Print the merged effective config as TOML and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LS_COLORS
Color information for filename categories and extensions (as produced by
dircolors(1)); a built-in scheme is used when unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color output.
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
Force color output.
.TP
.B TOW_CONFIG
Path to a config file, used instead of the default user config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tow/config.toml
User config (default \fI~/.config/tow/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.I .tow.toml
Project config, discovered by walking up from the current directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
tree(1), ls(1), git(1), strftime(3), glob(7)
